id: hac-r2z9
title: Add coalesced WebSocket trigger subscriptions
description: "Implement the latest stable Home Assistant WebSocket supported-features negotiation and typed subscribe_trigger workflow so agents can observe automation triggers with bounded, token-efficient output."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 0
tags[5]: agents,automation,home-assistant,streaming,websocket
created_at: "2026-07-25T00:16:24.568Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T00:16:24.568Z"
deadline: "2026-08-01T00:16:24.568Z"
assignee: unbraind
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "The client negotiates coalesce_messages as command id 1 immediately after authentication and correctly dispatches both single-object and coalesced-array frames; hassio ws subscribe-trigger accepts inline JSON or a JSON file, optional variables, bounded wait/max-event controls, and provides detailed examples and global help; Trigger subscriptions validate input before network I/O, unsubscribe reliably, preserve generic passthrough, and remain read-only safe; All source coverage remains 100/100/100/100, docstrings remain complete, every source file stays within 300 code lines, and all formatter/help/schema/live/release/security/PM gates pass"
definition_of_ready: Official docs and current Core source agree; live read-only negotiation and trigger subscription succeed; all-status PM search finds no duplicate
goal: best-agent-home-assistant-cli
objective: bounded-token-efficient-automation-observation
value: Let agents observe meaningful automation conditions instead of consuming the entire event bus.
impact: Reduces framing and token overhead while adding a stable typed streaming primitive.
outcome: A production-ready typed trigger subscription surface with coalesced protocol handling and exact-head delivery proof.
why_now: "The stable latest API documents subscribe_trigger and coalescing, but the existing CLI cannot use the former or decode the latter."
parent: hac-4s9j
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 98
sprint: 2026-07-websocket-streaming
release: 2026.7.25
